### Check 4 — Security high findings

{% if light_check | default(false) %}Gate on the scan's own stdout, not on a file: `Security scan: N finding(s)` and, when N > 0,
the `Severity: high=K, …` line after it (`<severity>=<count>` pairs, comma-separated).
- N = 0 → PASS.
- N > 0 with a missing or unparseable `Severity:` line → not a pass.
- A count above 0 for `high` or `P0` → not a pass: a finding this scan just printed carries no
  recorded resolution yet, so review runs next.
- Otherwise PASS.

The scan's rows are the last N lines of `{{ WTR }}/.claude/observability/security/findings-<today>.jsonl`
(`<today>` is the UTC date, `date -u +%F`); read them for detail only. The file's earlier lines
are earlier scans'.{% else %}Read the most recent `.claude/observability/security/findings-*.jsonl`.{% endif %}

FAIL when: any finding has `severity == "high"` AND `resolution != "accepted-risk-with-rationale"`. Resolutions must be deliberate (recorded in PLAN ADR or wrapup commit body).

PASS when: zero unresolved high findings.
